# What the `.dbd` does not carry: the type AND the `special` of a
# `special(SPC_DBADDR)` field. Same grammar and same purpose as
# `crates/epics-base-rs/dbd/cvt_dbaddr.types` — read that file's header for the
# reasoning; this one covers only the record types declared in THIS crate's
# `dbd/` directory.
#
# sscanRecord.c's `cvt_dbaddr` types every detector array (DnnDA, DnnCA) as
# DBF_FLOAT and every positioner array (PnPA, PnRA, PnCA) as DBF_DOUBLE, `MPTS`
# deep, unconditionally, and never touches `paddr->special`.
#
# record.FIELD          DBF type        special     dyn         size    C source
